  "comment": "kiln.content: the game's registries (items, recipes, random-loot items, default-inventory drop tables), the game's own reflection (TypeByHash) for their layouts, and the inventory stack-size clamp. Typed holes capture every registry offset the service relies on; see docs/re/content.md. New content (content.new): the item map insert as ItemRegistryUpdate phase 1 does it (items.map2 = the map it inserts into), the recipe registry's workshop map (+recipes.workshops, values SmallDynamicArray<RecipeInfo*, ws_max> of ws_stride bytes, u16 count at +ws_count). New items in random loot (content.loot_new): every roll builds its candidate list from the LootableItemsResource items array, read through the getter LootItems ({data, count} of lootRegistry+lootreg.data -> +loot.items); kiln.content hooks it to append new items' LootableItemInfo copies and inserts them into the loot map (LootFind), docs/re/content.md 8.4.",
